{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01371",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 1.13,
      "end_seconds": 4.65,
      "duration_seconds": 3.52,
      "text": "right, hello, good to see you please sit"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 6.59,
      "end_seconds": 7.62,
      "duration_seconds": 1.03,
      "text": "hi, thanks"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 8.34,
      "end_seconds": 14.56,
      "duration_seconds": 6.22,
      "text": "Hello, doctor. I hope it's alright if I stay in for this."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 15.97,
      "end_seconds": 19.24,
      "duration_seconds": 3.27,
      "text": "So what can I do for you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 20.61,
      "end_seconds": 26.11,
      "duration_seconds": 5.5,
      "text": "doctor, it's pain low in the pelvis that's what we're worried about"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 27.12,
      "end_seconds": 36.54,
      "duration_seconds": 9.42,
      "text": "tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 38.48,
      "end_seconds": 42.41,
      "duration_seconds": 3.93,
      "text": "I'd say every other day. Mostly severe."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 43.06,
      "end_seconds": 49.92,
      "duration_seconds": 6.86,
      "text": "And the other thing I wanted to mention is that that I can't really—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 50.02,
      "end_seconds": 55.26,
      "duration_seconds": 5.24,
      "text": "Yeah tell the doctor about the other thing that's what worries me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 57.3,
      "end_seconds": 67.17,
      "duration_seconds": 9.87,
      "text": "I was getting to that! Oh, and pain during sex that's been about the same, about a week"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 67.74,
      "end_seconds": 69.48,
      "duration_seconds": 1.74,
      "text": "any bloating as well?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 70.21,
      "end_seconds": 74.56,
      "duration_seconds": 4.35,
      "text": "Yeah. About four days, uh, I'd say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 76.29,
      "end_seconds": 79.58,
      "duration_seconds": 3.29,
      "text": "How much trouble does it give you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 81.43,
      "end_seconds": 83.11,
      "duration_seconds": 1.68,
      "text": "I'd say moderate"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 83.69,
      "end_seconds": 90.14,
      "duration_seconds": 6.45,
      "text": "Have you had pain low in the pelvis before, or is this the first time?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 91.32,
      "end_seconds": 96.51,
      "duration_seconds": 5.19,
      "text": "A bit, last year. It settled by itself back then."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 98.1,
      "end_seconds": 101.54,
      "duration_seconds": 3.44,
      "text": "Do you take any prescribed or over-the-counter medicines?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 103.34,
      "end_seconds": 110.72,
      "duration_seconds": 7.38,
      "text": "Naproxen, 250 milligrams, twice a day. Glibenclamide. I take it 5 milligrams, before breakfast"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 111.36,
      "end_seconds": 121.1,
      "duration_seconds": 9.74,
      "text": "Doctor uh I think the last prescription for the glibenclamide was 2.5 milligrams. We changed it at the last visit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 121.97,
      "end_seconds": 126.33,
      "duration_seconds": 4.36,
      "text": "I see. Is the most recent prescription on you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 128.01,
      "end_seconds": 147.82,
      "duration_seconds": 19.81,
      "text": "not with me i'll bring it next time it's escitalopram, 10 milligrams, once a day i didn't want to make a fuss, you know. Mefenamic acid i take it 500 milligrams, when it hurts i was on Glycomet before i stopped taking it"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 148.82,
      "end_seconds": 149.6,
      "duration_seconds": 0.78,
      "text": "any smoking?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 150.77,
      "end_seconds": 154.4,
      "duration_seconds": 3.63,
      "text": "I have about eight cigarettes in a day"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 155.82,
      "end_seconds": 157.51,
      "duration_seconds": 1.69,
      "text": "who lives with you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 158.49,
      "end_seconds": 161.27,
      "duration_seconds": 2.78,
      "text": "My partner and our baby"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 162.9,
      "end_seconds": 167.48,
      "duration_seconds": 4.58,
      "text": "Do you react to any medicines or foods? Any allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 168.63,
      "end_seconds": 172.07,
      "duration_seconds": 3.44,
      "text": "no, not that I know of"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 172.63,
      "end_seconds": 179.06,
      "duration_seconds": 6.43,
      "text": "I'm, I'm not sure that's right. I seem to recall a problem with erythromycin."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 180.17,
      "end_seconds": 183.34,
      "duration_seconds": 3.17,
      "text": "really? I don't think so so"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 185.31,
      "end_seconds": 192.45,
      "duration_seconds": 7.14,
      "text": "Right, fair enough, I'll write down both versions. What about your parents, brothers or sisters, any conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 195.59,
      "end_seconds": 200.43,
      "duration_seconds": 4.84,
      "text": "my aunt has rheumatoid arthritis. My cousin has psoriasis"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 202.29,
      "end_seconds": 205.54,
      "duration_seconds": 3.25,
      "text": "Has anyone ever diagnosed you with something?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 206.34,
      "end_seconds": 209.95,
      "duration_seconds": 3.61,
      "text": "Arthritis in my knees, for five years"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 210.52,
      "end_seconds": 211.98,
      "duration_seconds": 1.46,
      "text": "yes, carry on"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 213.49,
      "end_seconds": 215.99,
      "duration_seconds": 2.5,
      "text": "Diabetes for about ten years"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 216.96,
      "end_seconds": 217.98,
      "duration_seconds": 1.02,
      "text": "Hm, okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 218.64,
      "end_seconds": 228.87,
      "duration_seconds": 10.23,
      "text": "I've had anxiety for nearly five years now i thought it would sort itself out, but it hasn't"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 230.37,
      "end_seconds": 231.66,
      "duration_seconds": 1.29,
      "text": "any other things?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 233.71,
      "end_seconds": 244.93,
      "duration_seconds": 11.22,
      "text": "Right, so anxiety is already on your record. We'll keep that in mind today. Let me check a few things. Any vaginal discharge, fever or bleeding between periods?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 246.69,
      "end_seconds": 261.43,
      "duration_seconds": 14.74,
      "text": "No no vaginal discharge no fever no bleeding between periods. I did have a lot of tiredness at one point but that went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 262.35,
      "end_seconds": 268.1,
      "duration_seconds": 5.75,
      "text": "let me check a few things. Any vomiting or burning when passing urine?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 268.85,
      "end_seconds": 273.75,
      "duration_seconds": 4.9,
      "text": "no vomiting or burning when passing urine, none of it"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 274.04,
      "end_seconds": 278.75,
      "duration_seconds": 4.71,
      "text": "I see go ahead. How are your joints any aches elsewhere?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 280.28,
      "end_seconds": 282.23,
      "duration_seconds": 1.95,
      "text": "I move fine otherwise."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_5",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 291.52,
      "end_seconds": 301.19,
      "duration_seconds": 9.67,
      "text": "Okay, so the vitals from earlier. SpO2 98 percent on room air, pressure 128 over 75. Temperature 36.6, pulse 68."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 303.17,
      "end_seconds": 305.08,
      "duration_seconds": 1.91,
      "text": "So, good, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 306.65,
      "end_seconds": 308.86,
      "duration_seconds": 2.21,
      "text": "may I examine you now?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 310.67,
      "end_seconds": 311.96,
      "duration_seconds": 1.29,
      "text": "nearly finished here"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 319.73,
      "end_seconds": 325.75,
      "duration_seconds": 6.02,
      "text": "There's tenderness in the lower tummy on the left, and no guarding."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 327.93,
      "end_seconds": 346.49,
      "duration_seconds": 18.56,
      "text": "Please sit back down. Putting it all together, I'd lean towards chronic pelvic pain, possibly endometriosis. That's my thinking for now, and it may change as we learn more. An ovarian cyst is also on my list. A A pelvic infection is also on my list."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 350.54,
      "end_seconds": 351.96,
      "duration_seconds": 1.42,
      "text": "is this permanent?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 353.55,
      "end_seconds": 362.83,
      "duration_seconds": 9.28,
      "text": "I can't promise yet, but most people with chronic pelvic pain, possibly endometriosis do well once it's treated properly"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 373.41,
      "end_seconds": 377.21,
      "duration_seconds": 3.8,
      "text": "I'm gonna order a pregnancy test, for pelvic pain"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 378.4,
      "end_seconds": 379.32,
      "duration_seconds": 0.92,
      "text": "Mm alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 380.17,
      "end_seconds": 405.44,
      "duration_seconds": 25.27,
      "text": "Let's book a pelvic ultrasound to look into pelvic pain. A heat pad and some gentle movement help many people, and a pain diary helps me see a pattern. And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose. We'll catch up in four weeks. Does all of that make sense?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 409.1,
      "end_seconds": 412.17,
      "duration_seconds": 3.07,
      "text": "Alright um thanks take care."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 413.92,
      "end_seconds": 415.14,
      "duration_seconds": 1.22,
      "text": "all the best"
    }
  ]
}